WEBVTT

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.500
Mister!

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:19.700
Stay back!

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.000
Is this... a mermaid?

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:34.700
Goldfish...

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.330
It's a goldfish all right.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:49.950
"The Ones Within"

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:14.540
It's so big... I wonder if it's mutated.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:21.040
Look by the dorsal fin! It almost
looks like a person's face!

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.250
Let's head back.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:27.200
Be careful, Mister!
That part gets pretty deep!

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.540
This way!

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:33.000
You know your way around.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.700
Because I come here in secret all the time.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:40.580
Now I know why her
brother's always worried...

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:52.000
Mister?

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.450
Mister!

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:05.500
Welcome back, Hiro. Did you find Sakura?

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.080
She's gone...

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:13.160
She's not in her room, the shower,
or even the mushroom spot!

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:15.120
Sakura!

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:18.870
Well, she's probably on
one of her adventures again.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.080
Where's he at?

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:24.700
If you mean Onigasaki, I had him
go look around the waterway.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:25.660
--Nanami, you big idiot!

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.700
--Wh-Whoa, careful now!
--Nanami, you big idiot!

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:30.950
What if Sakura ends up alone with him?!

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:34.580
--That's a good thing. They can get
along and walk back together.
--He's a huge pervert!

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:38.540
Get along?! You're unbelievable, Nanami!

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:39.910
I've gotta go!

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:41.330
Wait right there!

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.040
I'm coming, too.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:05.290
So, what's this rhythm
thing you're on about?

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:07.080
It's "Luhn algorithm."

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.450
Huh?

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:12.330
One you might be familiar with
is credit card numbers.

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:17.250
At first glance, you might think they're
random, but certain rules apply to it.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:21.620
Look here. I'll make it easy
to understand with a 5x10 puzzle.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:26.160
"Puzzle"
The only numbers that conform
to the algorithm are in the very first row.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.950
It goes 10, 20, 30 and increases.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:29.330
"Ascending"
It goes 10, 20, 30 and increases.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:29.910
"Ascending"
After the first row, the numbers are random...

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.500
"Puzzle"
After the first row, the numbers are random...

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:31.950
"Random"
After the first row, the numbers are random...

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.660
"Random"
...but they're never larger
than the next column over.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:37.250
"Random"
In other words, a piece conforming
to the algorithm or not...

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:37.830
"Conforms to algorithm"
In other words, a piece conforming
to the algorithm or not...

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:40.910
"Conforms to algorithm"
"(Doesn't conform to algorithm)"
...lets you determine if it's
horizontal or vertical.

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:42.950
"Conforms to algorithm"
"(Doesn't conform to algorithm)"
What matters is knowing that 5x10
is the number of row and column pieces.

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:46.830
"Puzzle"
What matters is knowing that 5x10
is the number of row and column pieces.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:49.580
If we split the puzzle up
into vertical sections,

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:52.250
we can determine the
piece that doesn't belong.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:55.500
That's because only one of the
columns will have an extra piece.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:59.950
Once we assemble that specific column,
the piece left over is...

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.540
...the correct password!

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:12.830
I can't breathe!

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:30.160
This way, Mister!

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.290
Get down!

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:59.290
How nostalgic...
You're alive after all this time?

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:00.910
You know what that is?

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:02.660
Yeah.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:07.160
One of the tests four years ago was
something called "Goldfish Scooping."

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:10.700
This fellow was the target back then.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:14.830
I must say, it used to be a lot more adorable.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.000
Come, let's head back.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.040
Warn us before you do that!

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.450
Hey, it's still following us.

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:39.000
Oh, that's because you look
tasty and it fancies you.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.660
Quit saying stuff like that!

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:51.120
You sure you can manage on your own?

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.830
No sweat!

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:57.290
We're done splitting the puzzle up
and all that's left is to build it.

00:06:57.290 --> 00:07:01.500
And sorry, but I can
concentrate better alone.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:07.080
But if you insist, leave Karirin
behind as a body pillow for me.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:08.330
Huh?

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:10.500
You might want to reconsider--

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:14.080
Because-- she-- sometimes--

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:17.250
smacks-- you-- with a-- back-- hand--

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:19.040
I'll be careful, meow.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:23.750
In the rare chance that I somehow fail,

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:27.580
I want you guys to try out
Anboy's last-ditch effort.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:31.000
But until then, go on and rest in your rooms.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.200
Akki and Makimaki haven't slept yet, right?

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.330
Y-You haven't either...

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:40.200
Yuzu...

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:41.750
Give it your best.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.370
Roromori.

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:51.200
Never mind... Good luck.

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:58.910
Doesn't it look like a person
when it's swimming?

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:01.160
That's why Niki called it a mermaid.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:02.160
Niki?

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:05.750
Oh, sorry. I mean my former partner.

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:08.540
We're the ones who dug that tunnel.

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:10.080
Oh?

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:14.620
And by the way, Sakura...

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:17.750
Don't you be dragging Onigasaki into trouble.

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:19.700
Huh? Uh...

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:22.830
It's fine if you go on adventures,
but tone it down.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:26.080
O-Okay... Sorry...

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:27.700
But...

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:34.330
Go on, go on. You have something
you want to give him, right?

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:37.500
Uh, let's not do this right now, Mister.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.040
It's for you.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:47.330
I knew you really wanted these parts, so...

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.330
Well...

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:52.660
Yes, I suppose I did.

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:55.290
Thank you, Sakura.

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:57.750
But please don't do anything crazy.

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:01.120
It would make me sad if you got hurt.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:05.330
Okay... Okay, I'll be careful!

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:06.910
Don't mind it.

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:08.500
What's with you?

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:19.830
I'm so sleepy, Karirin.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:22.790
N-Now, now...

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:26.200
You know what? I wanna dive into bed, too.

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:28.500
I wish I could dive into Akki.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:34.790
I-Is that right? The last half
sounds like nonsense, but okay...

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:37.450
You're almost there.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:39.660
Okay? Let's do our best?

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:40.950
Yeah.

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:45.540
What kind of roleplay was that?

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:47.950
You're the one who asked for this!

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:49.450
Achoo!

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:52.200
Oh, my, what a cute sneeze.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.000
I'm freezing...

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:58.290
Sorry, Sakura should
be done in the shower soon.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:08.870
Um...

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:14.660
Is there anything I can help with?

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:16.000
Nope.

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:20.000
No, but...

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:22.250
Just stay here with me.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:27.950
"Tuna" "Mackerel in Soy"
"Sardines" "Miso Broiled"
Wonder if I should return to the room?

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:29.250
"Tuna" "Mackerel in Soy"
"Sardines" "Miso Broiled"
The White Room?

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:30.410
The White Room?

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:35.750
I think there's nothing to worry about.
He has no interest in dropouts.

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:39.120
Give me lots of sugar.

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:40.950
Pour me some milk.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:42.370
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:48.160
Nothing happened when
Hiro and I escaped either.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:51.080
Maybe the surveillance cameras didn't see us?

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:55.540
Are you sure he's not just pulling our strings?

00:10:57.250 --> 00:11:00.370
Meaning he already knows
about the escape route...

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:04.200
...and is using me as bait to capture
the dropouts in one fell swoop.

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:10.250
It's possible... In which case,
we'll put up a fight.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:13.250
Which is why we could use your strength.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:16.750
Onigasaki. Would you become our comrade?

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:20.000
No way.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.500
Huh?!

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:26.790
Sorry, but hiding around
doesn't suit me very well.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:31.160
I'd rather just go on my own
and do as I please.

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:36.790
All right. But in exchange,
let's trade information once in a while.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:39.830
Achoo!

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:42.870
Oh, my, isn't your face a little red?

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:51.540
Shoot, when did I...?

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:56.540
Yuzu!

00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:59.120
Sorry, I threw up.

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:01.620
I'm just a bit anemic.

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:03.790
I'll go and get someone to help!

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:05.080
I'm fine.

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:07.910
You're not! Please, just lie down!

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:18.080
Karirin was crying...

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:20.540
I need to get up soon...

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:23.290
I hate being alone...

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:25.660
I want to touch someone...

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:48.450
Big Sis...

00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:14.790
You owe me one, Roromori.

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:25.830
Don't forget who your
master is ever again, Recorder.

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:33.660
Seven point eight.

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:38.160
You must be pretty delicate to end up
like this from getting a little wet.

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:45.250
Uh, I-I bet you're just tired from
being somewhere you're not used to!

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:48.620
"Tower Blueprints"
Huh? That's...

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:49.700
"Tower Blueprints"
Oh...

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:50.870
Oh...

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:53.160
Omejima gave these to me.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:55.120
"Tower Blueprints"

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:56.120
"Tower Blueprints"
But still, holding onto these for four years...

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:59.540
But still, holding onto these for four years...

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:04.450
I don't think Nanami has given up yet
when it comes to his partner.

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:08.500
I think he still believes
he'll come back and rescue him.

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:12.330
What do you plan on doing?

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:13.250
Huh?

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:16.660
Will you come with me?
You can meet your brother.

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:28.160
Password confirmed.

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:32.750
Lock to special section B-13
has been released.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:40.450
Hiro probably wouldn't
want to leave Nanami behind.

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:43.830
That's how he was when I dropped out.

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:49.450
He purposely dropped out with me
thinking I'd be lonely all alone.

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:55.120
Zakuro is my family,
so I want to see him, but...

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:59.790
Hiro and Nanami are pretty much
the same now... and I can't leave them.

00:15:06.700 --> 00:15:08.500
Crap, there's an emergency!

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:13.790
The White Room! People came to the
White Room and are calling your name!

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:19.080
Onigasaki! Onigasaki!

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:23.540
Kaikoku, are you all right?!

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:24.870
Onigasaki!

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:26.080
There's no answer!

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:28.160
Wh-What if he collapsed?

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:30.910
What a pain in the ass! Let's kick the door in!

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:34.000
Onigasaki, we'll wait ten more seconds.

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.830
Oh, no... These kids are so extreme...

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:39.250
Hiro, bring him here quick!

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:45.410
I've got to buy some time... I know!

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:48.120
Oh, there's paper sliding under the door.

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:49.080
"Occupied"

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:50.000
"Occupied"
Onigasaki?

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:54.540
"Occupied"
Huh? Is it really Kaikoku?
The writing's so round and cute!

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:57.950
"It's me, Onigasaki"
Wait, there's another one... This is weird!

00:15:57.950 --> 00:15:59.580
Kaikoku!

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:02.040
Argh, it had the opposite effect!

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:05.120
Shh.

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:11.450
Kaikoku, I want you to listen to me.

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:15.830
After you left, we finished
a dropout rescue game.

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:20.290
Kaikoku, you'll be able to participate in the--

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:24.910
Onigasaki.

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:31.040
Roromori's resting in the infirmary right now.

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:33.410
Roro is?

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:36.830
She tackled the puzzle so hard
for you, she collapsed.

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:47.790
Come back! We're all waiting for you!

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:56.250
Say something! Hey, Onigasaki!

00:16:56.250 --> 00:16:59.660
Open up! Please! Hey!

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:02.370
Onigasaki, open up!

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.500
Keep this a secret from Zakuro.

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:16.080
He's bad at hiding emotions.

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:25.620
See you later.

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:34.410
Kaikoku!

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:37.660
Yeah, my bad. Sorry for making you--

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:39.290
What was that for?

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:42.120
Because you deserve it.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:46.040
I'm afraid I don't follow what you mean.

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:48.330
S-Sorry!

00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:53.290
Wh-What the hell is this about?

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:55.540
It's a welcome ritual!

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:07.790
You learned your lesson, right?

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:10.330
Don't pull anything like that again.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.870
Oshigiri, lend me your hand a sec.

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:26.290
Why?

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:27.790
Just do it.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:33.120
O-Onigasaki?

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:35.870
I'm so glad you're all right.

00:18:35.870 --> 00:18:39.790
Huh? Uh, um... Y-Yeah...

00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:50.290
Sorry, Sakura. I don't think
your message got through.

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:02.950
Welcome back, Kai.

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:04.700
I'm back.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.370
How are you feeling?

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:11.750
As you can see, I'm pretty good.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:17.120
But my nurse here won't agree
to discharge me just yet.

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:19.910
I'll join the others by tomorrow.

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:24.540
I heard from Iride and Oshigiri...

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:27.120
Said you were kinda reckless.

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:31.200
It's fine. This happening
was partially my fault, too.

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:39.330
You have questions for me, right? I'm all ears.

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:45.120
I found some strange documents in your room.

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:49.910
"--ground Report" "Name: Kaikoku Onigasaki"
"--ground Report" "Name: Zakuro Oshigiri"
There was all sorts of information
about the rest of us.

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:54.700
I knew it had to be you.

00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:58.750
I noticed the tilt on my photos
of Akki were slightly off.

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:02.830
Figured somebody must have
entered while I was away.

00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:06.750
"Notes
Grandpa Kaiun: Critical Condition"

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:10.200
Those documents... They're recent...

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:11.620
Are the things about my Grandpa--

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:13.250
It's true.

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:17.910
I'm sorry for keeping quiet.

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:22.330
I'm... I'm this game's record keeper.

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:25.040
I'm on Mr. Alpaca's side.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:31.410
Having said that, I'm something
like a monitor on the inside.

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:34.290
I only pass information on to Mr. Alpaca though.

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:35.200
"--ground Report" "Name: Anya Kudou"
"--ground Report" "Name: Himiko Inaba"
"--ground Report" "Name: Zakuro Oshigiri"
I only pass information on to Mr. Alpaca though.

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:37.700
"--ground Report" "Name: Anya Kudou"
"--ground Report" "Name: Himiko Inaba"
"--ground Report" "Name: Zakuro Oshigiri"
The details of everyone's participation...

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:41.410
"--ground Report" "Name: Karin Sarayashiki"
"--ground Report" "Name: Himiko Inaba"
Every person's thoughts and
feelings, progress, results...

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:44.870
All I learn through my own participation...

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:50.330
I took on the job out of pure curiosity.

00:20:50.330 --> 00:20:54.040
As you already know,
I'm pretty obsessed with Akki.

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:59.160
I was glad to do anything just
to get more information about him.

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:01.750
I was glad, but...

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:05.620
Why is it?

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:09.450
I didn't want the game to continue like that...

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:13.200
It's understandable that you would doubt me.

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:19.040
Even I can tell my behavior's suspicious, but...

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:22.660
...I'm not sure how long
I can play the clown though.

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:30.330
You decide what to do...
with the documents... and me.

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:36.660
I'm awful at dealing with things like this.

00:21:36.660 --> 00:21:39.080
All I want to know...

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:43.910
...is whether you're going
to be a friend or foe. That's all.

00:21:43.910 --> 00:21:46.750
If it's the former, we can
get back to talking gossip.

00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:51.330
If it's the latter, I'll punish you first
and then we'll get to the gossip.

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:57.370
You sure like gossip, don't you, Kai?

00:21:57.370 --> 00:22:02.790
Yeah... Because you're about
the only one I can chat with.

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:06.870
Which is why... Let's call a truce for now.

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:09.700
If you think of an answer, let me know.

00:22:18.790 --> 00:22:19.950
Right.

00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:17.000
Onigasaki! So this is where you were!

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:21.330
Why did you leave without saying?
I told you to quit doing that!

00:23:21.330 --> 00:23:24.290
You are one emotionally unstable boy.

00:23:24.290 --> 00:23:26.790
Who are you calling unstable, huh?!

00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:28.830
Yeah, yeah...

00:23:28.830 --> 00:23:32.790
--See you tomorrow, Roro.
--Don't push me! Hey, quit it!

00:23:34.540 --> 00:23:37.410
Yeah, thanks...

00:23:37.410 --> 00:23:39.000
See you tomorrow.
